## Commands

Node.js and pnpm, at the version `packageManager` names in `package.json`. Run `pnpm install` first.

- `pnpm lint`: oxlint, then ESLint{{ ', then stylelint' if design_system }}{{ ', then publint and attw on the packed package' if publish }}. It fixes what it can, so commit what it changes.
- `pnpm format`: formats everything with oxfmt. `pnpm format:check` only checks.
- `pnpm type-check`: type-checks everything.
- `pnpm test`: the unit tests, with Vitest.
{%- if browser_tests %}
- `pnpm test:browser`: builds {{ 'the ' ~ kind ~ ' and tests it' if kind != 'library' else 'the docs app and tests it' if docs_dir else 'the project and tests its own pages' }} in a browser, with Playwright.
{%- endif %}
- `pnpm build`: builds {{ 'the package' if kind == 'library' else 'the ' ~ kind }}{{ ' and the docs app' if docs_dir }}.

CI runs `format:check`, `lint`, `type-check`, `test` and `build`{{ ', then the browser tests' if browser_tests }}, and fails when `lint` changed a file. Run them before you push.

## Layout

{% if workspace == 'monorepo' -%}
- `{{ member_dir }}/`: {{ package_name }}, with its `src/` and `tests/`
{%- if docs_dir %}
- `{{ docs_dir }}/`: the docs app, deployed to GitHub Pages
{%- endif %}
{%- else -%}
- `src/`: the source
- `tests/`: the unit tests
{%- endif %}
{%- if browser_tests %}
- `tests/browser/`: the browser tests
{%- endif %}
- `.github/workflows/`: CI{{ ', the release' if publish }}{{ ', the GitHub Pages deployment' if pages }}, calling the shared workflows of whatsaaaa/template
{%- endif %}

## House rules

- Never use the em dash. Use a plain dash (-) instead.
{%- set generated = ['`.copier-answers.yml`'] + (['`pnpm-lock.yaml`'] if typescript else []) + (['`CHANGELOG.md`'] if publish else []) %}
- Never edit a generated file by hand: {{ generated | join(', ') }} and anything else a tool writes. Change its source and run the tool instead.
{%- if publish %}
- A change to what the package ships adds a changeset (`pnpm changeset`), which writes the release notes. Never bump the version by hand.
{%- endif %}
- The shared files come from the template, [whatsaaaa/template](https://github.com/whatsaaaa/template), and `copier update` brings its changes. A change that every project should have goes to the template.
- Commits are signed. No commit or pull request carries an AI or agent attribution line.

